# dhclient — real-world examples

## Release the current IP address

```sh
sudo dhclient -r
```

## Obtain a new IP address

```sh
sudo dhclient
```

Running release then obtain is the common way to refresh a lease.

## Target a specific interface

```sh
sudo dhclient eth0
```

## Verbose output when troubleshooting a lease

```sh
sudo dhclient -v eth0
```

## Homelab: bounce the lease after changing a static reservation on the router

```sh
sudo dhclient -r eth0 && sudo dhclient -v eth0
ip addr show eth0   # confirm the new address
```

## Note for OpenSUSE Tumbleweed

NetworkManager usually owns DHCP on desktop installs. Prefer:

```sh
nmcli device reapply eth0
# or bounce the connection entirely
nmcli connection down "Wired connection 1" && nmcli connection up "Wired connection 1"
```

| Flag | What it does              |
| ---- | ------------------------- |
| -r   | release current lease     |
| -v   | verbose output            |
| -x   | stop the running client   |
